# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Arca — environment
# Copy to `.env.local`. Every value here is optional: with none of them set the
# app boots against the in-memory fixture repository, which is how you develop
# the UI without a database. See backend/db/repository.ts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PostgreSQL. Set this and the app switches from fixtures to the real
# object-graph schema. Vercel Postgres and Neon both hand you this string.
#
# IMPORTANT: setting this is a commitment, not a preference. The app does not
# fall back to fixtures when the database is unreachable — falling back would
# mean a running app quietly serving different data than the one it was
# configured for, and a sign-in that "worked" against a store that forgets
# everything on restart. It says the database is down instead.
#
# So if you set this, the database has to be up:
#
#   docker compose up -d      # start it
#   npm run db:migrate        # create the tables
#   npm run db:seed           # the campaign, its members and their inventory
#
# Unset it (or comment it out) to go back to fixtures.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://arca:arca@127.0.0.1:5432/arca

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign-in
#
# There is nothing to configure. Arca has no OAuth provider and no mail server:
# sign-in is an email address and a password (backend/lib/password.ts), and
# there are two ways to get an account.
#
#   /signup   anyone with the link, and it always produces a PLAYER.
#   /members  the GM, who may seat a player OR another GM.
#
# Neither sends mail. There is no address confirmation and no password-reset
# link, because sending either needs an SMTP provider and credentials this app
# deliberately does not carry. Recovery is the GM clearing a password from
# /members, which puts that member back at "choose a password" — the same state
# a newly added one starts in. As one statement, if you would rather not sign
# in as the GM:
#
#   UPDATE users SET password_hash = NULL WHERE email = 'kova@ravenholt.example';
#
# With fixtures (no DATABASE_URL) every member starts unenrolled and the whole
# store resets whenever the server restarts, which is why `npm run dev` needs
# no database and no configuration at all — and why nothing you do in that mode
# is kept.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The campaign this deployment serves. One campaign per deployment for now
# (SCOPE.md §13 Q5).
# ARCA_CAMPAIGN_ID=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
